INSERT INTO `practice_sets` VALUES (1,1,6,5,NULL,'flashcards','Flashcards: Making inferences while reading',NULL,'[{\"front\":\"What is an inference?\",\"back\":\"A logical conclusion reached by combining text clues with what you already know.\",\"source\":1,\"source_ref\":{\"title\":\"Making inferences while reading\",\"where\":\"What an inference is\",\"material_id\":8}},{\"front\":\"What formula helps create an inference?\",\"back\":\"Text clues + what I know = inference.\",\"source\":2,\"source_ref\":{\"title\":\"Making inferences while reading\",\"where\":\"Clues plus knowledge\",\"material_id\":8}},{\"front\":\"List the first three steps for making an inference.\",\"back\":\"1) Ask a question the text doesn’t answer directly. 2) Find two or three clues in the text. 3) Connect the clues to what you already know.\",\"source\":3,\"source_ref\":{\"title\":\"Making inferences while reading\",\"where\":\"Steps for making an inference\",\"material_id\":8}},{\"front\":\"What can we infer about Mara in the practice passage?\",\"back\":\"She is worried about being late, even though she lets older women board first.\",\"source\":4,\"source_ref\":{\"title\":\"Making inferences while reading\",\"where\":\"A short practice passage\",\"material_id\":8}},{\"front\":\"Name one common mistake when making an inference.\",\"back\":\"Making a guess that has no support in the text.\",\"source\":5,\"source_ref\":{\"title\":\"Making inferences while reading\",\"where\":\"Common mistakes\",\"material_id\":8}}]','ai','[{\"known\":true},{\"known\":false},{\"known\":true},{\"known\":false},{\"known\":true}]',3,5,'2026-10-22 19:50:45','2026-10-22 19:50:45','2026-10-21 00:39:02','2026-10-22 19:50:45'),(2,1,6,3,6,'flashcards','Flashcards: Quadratic equations: four methods',NULL,'[{\"front\":\"What is the standard form of a quadratic equation?\",\"back\":\"ax² + bx + c = 0, where a, b, c are real numbers and a ≠ 0.\",\"source\":1,\"source_ref\":{\"title\":\"Quadratic equations: four methods\",\"where\":\"What makes an equation quadratic\",\"material_id\":6}},{\"front\":\"When is the extracting square roots method appropriate?\",\"back\":\"When the equation has no x term (b = 0).\",\"source\":2,\"source_ref\":{\"title\":\"Quadratic equations: four methods\",\"where\":\"Method 1: Extracting square roots\",\"material_id\":6}},{\"front\":\"What property lets you solve a factored quadratic like (x + 2)(x + 3) = 0?\",\"back\":\"Zero product property: if pq = 0, then p = 0 or q = 0.\",\"source\":3,\"source_ref\":{\"title\":\"Quadratic equations: four methods\",\"where\":\"Method 2: Factoring\",\"material_id\":6}},{\"front\":\"What does the discriminant b² − 4ac tell you?\",\"back\":\"If >0: two distinct real roots; =0: one repeated real root; <0: no real roots.\",\"source\":6,\"source_ref\":{\"title\":\"Quadratic equations: four methods\",\"where\":\"The discriminant\",\"material_id\":6}},{\"front\":\"Write the quadratic formula.\",\"back\":\"x = [‑b ± √(b² ‑ 4ac)] \\/ (2a).\",\"source\":5,\"source_ref\":{\"title\":\"Quadratic equations: four methods\",\"where\":\"Method 4: The quadratic formula\",\"material_id\":6}}]','ai',NULL,NULL,5,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-21 00:39:40','2026-10-21 00:39:40');
