0,1.00,7.00,'graded',NULL,NULL,'released','2026-10-19 23:24:16',NULL,'2026-10-18 10:37:00','XGSX26TB27','2026-10-18 10:19:00','2026-10-20 23:24:16'),(9,1,1,16,1,1,'online','submitted',NULL,'2026-10-17 11:22:00','2026-10-20 23:44:16',NULL,'2026-10-17 11:40:00',0,3.00,3.00,7.00,'graded',NULL,NULL,'released','2026-10-19 23:24:16',NULL,'2026-10-17 11:40:00','9GKD9FPBKA','2026-10-17 11:22:00','2026-10-20 23:24:16'),(10,1,1,17,1,1,'online','submitted',NULL,'2026-10-16 12:25:00','2026-10-20 23:44:16',NULL,'2026-10-16 12:43:00',0,3.00,3.00,7.00,'graded',NULL,NULL,'released','2026-10-19 23:24:16',NULL,'2026-10-16 12:43:00','6BKT3PVDPV','2026-10-16 12:25:00','2026-10-20 23:24:16'),(11,1,2,8,2,1,'online','submitted','Resting: 16 breaths per minute. After jumping jacks: 34. After 5 minutes rest: 19.\n\nOur breathing rate more than doubled after exercise and almost returned to normal after resting. The leg muscles were using more oxygen for cellular respiration and making more carbon dioxide, so we breathed faster to bring in oxygen and remove CO2. My partner\'s pulse also went up, which means the heart pumped blood faster to carry the oxygen to the muscles.\n\nNext question: does breathing rate return to normal faster for students who exercise every day?','2026-10-19 09:15:00',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-19 10:05:00',0,NULL,NULL,10.00,'needs_review',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,NULL,NULL,'6V9MA8M7SF','2026-10-19 09:15:00','2026-10-19 10:05:00'),(12,1,2,12,2,1,'online','submitted','At rest 15, after exercise 31, after rest 18 breaths per minute.\n\nBreathing went up because the muscles needed more energy. The circulatory system moved blood faster too. Next I would test if holding your breath first changes the results.','2026-10-20 10:22:00',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-20 11:12:00',0,NULL,NULL,10.00,'needs_review',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,NULL,NULL,'6RKHDZWAX9','2026-10-20 10:22:00','2026-10-20 11:12:00'),(13,1,2,14,2,1,'online','submitted','Rest 17 / exercise 30 / recovery 20.\n\nWe breathed faster after exercising because the body needs more oxygen. Next time I want to measure heart rate also.','2026-10-19 11:29:00',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-19 12:19:00',0,NULL,NULL,10.00,'needs_review',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DNCNUYPN7Y','2026-10-19 11:29:00','2026-10-19 12:19:00'),(14,1,2,7,2,1,'online','submitted','Resting 18, after jumping jacks 29, after resting 22. Breathing increases when you exercise.','2026-10-20 12:36:00',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-20 13:26:00',0,NULL,NULL,10.00,'needs_review',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,NULL,NULL,'QCKAY6DSH4','2026-10-20 12:36:00','2026-10-20 13:26:00'),(15,1,2,16,2,1,'online','submitted','Data: 16, 33, 18. When we exercise the muscles need more oxygen and produce more carbon dioxide. The diaphragm works faster so more air comes in, and the heart beats faster so the blood carries the oxygen to the muscles quicker. Question: does the type of exercise matter?','2026-10-19 13:43:00',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-19 14:33:00',0,NULL,NULL,10.00,'needs_review',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,NULL,NULL,'MU52AGM34B','2026-10-19 13:43:00','2026-10-19 14:33:00'),(16,1,2,6,2,1,'online','submitted','Resting: 15 breaths per minute\nAfter jumping jacks: 32\nAfter 5 minutes rest: 17\n\nThe pattern: breathing rate doubled after exercise and went almost back to normal after resting.','2026-10-20 03:24:16',NULL,NULL,'2026-10-20 23:34:51',0,NULL,NULL,10.00,'needs_review',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,NULL,NULL,'8NKCT7YBSA','2026-10-20 03:24:16','2026-10-20 23:34:51'),(17,1,2,9,2,1,'online','in_progress','Rest 18, exercise 30','2026-10-19 23:24:16',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,10.00,'ungraded',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-19 23:24:16','2026-10-19 23:24:16'),(18,1,3,8,3,1,'online','submitted',NULL,'2026-10-20 22:26:16','2026-10-20 23:44:16',NULL,'2026-10-20 22:44:16',0,4.00,NULL,8.00,'needs_review',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,NULL,NULL,'8C626PGMPR','2026-10-20 22:26:16','2026-10-20 22:44:16'),(19,1,3,16,3,1,'online','submitted',NULL,'2026-10-20 21:51:16','2026-10-20 23:44:16',NULL,'2026-10-